{
  "summary": "Updates the `dumptxoutset` RPC to fail early if a rollback target block is not on the active chain, prevent concurrent invocations, and automatically clean up incomplete snapshot files on failure. An atomic guard serializes runs while managing prune locks and temporary file removal.",
  "problem": "Specifying a rollback target on a stale branch causes `dumptxoutset` to perform an expensive UTXO set copy and disconnect blocks down to the target height before failing. In addition, concurrent calls overwrite the same `.incomplete` file path, corrupting output and clobbering prune locks, while aborted or failed runs leave orphaned partial files on disk.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'The full UTXO set is copied and blocks are disconnected back from the tip only to fail when the target block height is reached.'",
    "PR description: 'both runs would write to <path>.incomplete, so the second dump to the same path corrupts the file the first one reports as successfully written. And also the prune lock has a fixed name, so the second run overwrites the first's height and the first to finish deletes the others lock mid-rollback.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
